_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Missing error handling in handleCreate.**

If `onCreate` throws an error, `setSaving(false)` and `onOpenChange(false)` won't be called, leaving the dialog in a stuck "saving" state. Wrap in try/catch/finally.


<details>
<summary>🔎 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   const handleCreate = async () => {
     if (!selectedRecipe) return;
     setSaving(true);
+    try {
       await onCreate({
         prep_recipe: selectedRecipe,
         target_yield: targetYield,
         target_yield_unit: targetUnit,
         scheduled_for: scheduledFor || undefined,
         notes,
       });
+      onOpenChange(false);
+    } catch (error) {
+      // Error handling is done by onCreate via toast
+      console.error('Failed to create production run:', error);
+    } finally {
-    setSaving(false);
-    onOpenChange(false);
+      setSaving(false);
+    }
   };
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In src/components/prep/NewProductionRunDialog.tsx around lines 49 to 61,
handleCreate currently awaits onCreate without error handling so a thrown error
leaves the dialog stuck in saving; wrap the await onCreate call in a
try/catch/finally block, set setSaving(true) before the try, call
setSaving(false) and onOpenChange(false) in the finally block to guarantee
cleanup, and in the catch either rethrow or surface the error (e.g., call an
error handler or show a toast) so the failure isn't silently swallowed.
```

</details>

