1) Treat service_role as a root secret — never expose it client‑side. Keep it only in trusted server environments (server APIs, serverless/edge functions, CI) and store in secure env vars with rotation/audit. [1][2][3]

2) Minimize use: design systems so normal app flows use the anon/auth keys + RLS. Reserve service_role only for admin/maintenance jobs that truly need to bypass RLS. Prefer alternatives where possible. [1][4]

